WEBVTT

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:13.860
Man, I give up.

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:16.040
That was kind of surprising.

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:19.320
Hey. I'm trembling a little right now.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:20.330
How come?

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:23.920
Fighting and conflict and 
dissidence and animosity...

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.360
It makes me so uncomfortable...

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:29.050
When I see it, I don't know how to handle it.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:32.510
Those are a few fairly advanced 
words you know, Yumoto.

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:35.660
Because they make me uncomfortable, 
I can remember them even better.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:38.280
It's like they're burned 
into my brain, I guess.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:40.580
It just makes me so uncomfortable.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:42.520
Well, I'm the same way.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.660
I want to live a life without conflict,

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:48.000
and I want that for the 
people around me, too.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.530
You said it.

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:52.530
Why did this have to happen, huh?

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:29.790
Everyone Loves Someone!

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:33.480
It's over! It's over!

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:35.250
Class is over!

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:38.600
Senpais, I just learned something!

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:41.180
Sea slug mating... it's incredible!

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:44.890
They're hermaphrodites, see...

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:48.340
They have a sexual organ on 
each end of their body...

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:51.810
Tell us more about sea slug mating!

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.810
I'd love to hear all about it!

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:54.990
Um, well,

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:57.660
sea slugs have both male 
and female sexual organs,

00:02:57.660 --> 00:02:59.440
so apparently, they can line up in a block,

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:02.340
innie to outie and innie to outie...

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:06.180
But instead of forming a train 
like you might be thinking,

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:09.290
they can actually join up in a big ring...

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:11.180
Wow, that's amazing!

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:13.080
How do you know that?

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:16.450
Well, I was talking with everyone...

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:18.120
It's love, of course!

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:22.200
Love connects people in a giant chain
that goes all the way into space!

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:23.300
Wow!

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.010
That's huge!

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.570
Um... Io-senpai?

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:29.780
Can I help you?

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:31.720
And Ryuu-senpai...

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:32.600
What do you want?

00:03:33.050 --> 00:03:34.560
What's wrong?

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:35.940
Why do you ask?

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:39.170
Well... you're acting... 
a little different...

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:40.660
Are we?

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:41.860
You think?

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:45.340
Io-senpai, what are your 
thoughts on hermaphroditism?

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:47.540
Like "Doubling up must improve 
their cost performance!"

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:49.740
"What economic efficiency!" Or something.

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:51.260
Yeah, that's true.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:54.830
You could run a calculation like 
that in a split second, right?

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:56.630
What is that supposed to mean?

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:57.640
Nothing.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:03:59.910
I'm not saying

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:01.760
"For someone so good at calculations, 
your bank balance has been slipping lately;

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:03.800
I hope you're okay," or anything like that.

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:06.900
Yes, because a little 
ebb and flow is natural.

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:09.800
But yeah, sea slugs are impressive.

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:12.350
They could have a date or a fling with 
anyone they meet anywhere, like someone else I know.

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:15.310
Are you saying I'm a sea slug?

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:17.900
Sea slugs are cute.

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:20.080
Cows are cute, too!

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:22.400
I like brown cows!

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.360
A lot more than the black and white kind.

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:28.980
For some reason, I just like brown better!

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:32.510
Although I like pandas because 
they're black and white...

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:35.700
I guess I'd be disappointed if 
they were just brown all over.

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:37.330
I wonder why that is?

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:39.470
Because then they'd be ordinary bears.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:44.420
It's a little early, but I'm going 
to head for the Kurotama Bath.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:46.050
Atsushi, you come with me.

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:47.450
You too, Yumoto.

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:49.510
O-Okay.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:51.670
Anyone else in?

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:52.770
No?

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.070
If not, let's head out.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:02.740
Excuse me!

00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:06.180
<i>This is a threat to the continued 
existence of the Battle Lovers!</i>

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:09.700
<i>I must do something to break the deadlock!</i>

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:13.300
<i>I call it Operation: Restoration of Love!</i>

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:14.660
Oh, right.

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:17.080
Wom-chan, want some candy?

00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:19.980
Thank you very much!

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:24.540
Wom-san prefers spinach, I believe.

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:27.800
I thought he hated sweets.

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:31.320
That's not why he took it.

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:35.730
Wom-san won't turn down anybody
who's trying to be nice.

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:41.350
Because he never lets anyone turn him down
when he's trying to be nice?

00:05:41.950 --> 00:05:46.900
I guess you can't get rich
unless you assume the worst of everybody.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:50.230
That's probably what's going on, 
and Wom-san's having a hard time,

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:52.830
being left in the middle like that.

00:05:53.030 --> 00:05:55.130
He could have just come with us.

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:57.910
Wom-san's the kind of guy 
who would stay, though.

00:05:57.910 --> 00:05:59.620
Yeah, since leaving them alone together

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:02.410
feels like it would bring things to a head.

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:04.480
What do you mean, "bring them to a head"?

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:05.550
That's not what I want!

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:10.750
But it's not like those two had 
anything in common to begin with.

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:11.860
Yeah.

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:14.040
They're a miraculous pair.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:16.020
It's a miracle they can be in the same room.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:19.980
Apparently they both had an awful 
first impression of each other, too.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:21.690
<b>Class 1-A</b>

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:21.690
Going Dutch?

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.170
No way.

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:24.720
The guy should pay.

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:26.660
How come?

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:28.120
Women's lib, man.

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:31.490
That gender theory stuff 
doesn't matter on a date.

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:34.350
How do you let a girl know you like her?

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:35.270
With words?

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:36.260
With actions?

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:38.150
Or with telepathy?

00:06:38.150 --> 00:06:41.960
That one's nice if you can 
do it, but most people can't.

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:46.920
So the simplest way is to just 
say "I'll pay for the date."

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:52.170
There's no girl who won't like 
having you pick up her cup of tea,

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:55.380
and it's a small price to pay to 
let her know you like her, right?

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:56.600
Y-Yeah!

00:06:57.460 --> 00:07:01.000
Well, my girlfriend never lets me pay, though.

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:04.130
See, this is what we call 
a benefit-cost ratio.

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:06.570
Sorry.

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:10.490
Is something I said amusing to you?

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:12.670
Not really.

00:07:12.670 --> 00:07:15.270
It was just funny to hear someone talk

00:07:15.270 --> 00:07:18.040
about benefit-cost ratios over 
something as silly as dating.

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:22.370
If you ask me, obsessing 
over money is much sillier.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:25.300
Oh, you've taken the time to learn who I am?

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:28.340
I'm not an investment, you know.
There are better uses of your time.

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:32.300
No, I just know you because you're so annoying.

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:36.300
So why did they both join the Defense Club?

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:37.940
Well...

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:41.730
<b>Earth Defense Club (lol)</b>

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:44.690
Yes?

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:47.900
Is this the Earth Defense Club?

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:47.900
<i>Is this Earth Defense Club thing for real?</i>

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:49.700
Y-Yeah...

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:50.360
Yes...

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:58.700
I was just happy to have a new member...

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:00.370
So you accepted them both?

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:01.390
Separately?

00:08:01.390 --> 00:08:04.880
Well, we didn't know they hated each other.

00:08:07.350 --> 00:08:08.780
Well, well.

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:14.610
Would you please stop getting in my face?

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:17.140
You're the one getting in my face!

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:19.850
I heard overly persistent 
men never get dates!

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:22.560
That's right, it's important 
to know when to quit!

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:25.630
The Defense Club is perfect for 
skipping class and napping.

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:27.270
Don't get in my way!

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:30.010
Sometimes I want to look at the 
markets in peace and quiet, too!

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:32.240
Why don't <i>you</i> quit instead?

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:33.450
I want to join the club!

00:08:35.350 --> 00:08:37.630
So what happened then?

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:40.800
Well, we couldn't not let them join the club.

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:44.960
Although the club itself hadn't 
been registered at that point...

00:08:45.390 --> 00:08:47.420
This new series is so funny!

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:50.840
As I thought, biotech 
stocks are on the rise.

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:52.840
I'll have to check the price 
movements in the future.

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:57.160
Hey, Atsushi...

00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:58.300
En-chan...

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:00.470
You heading home?

00:09:01.070 --> 00:09:02.880
I'll accompany you.

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:04.050
How come?

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:05.770
What do you mean, how come?

00:09:06.050 --> 00:09:08.680
What do you mean, what do I mean, how come?

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:11.780
What do you mean, what do I mean, 
what do you mean, how come?

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:14.860
It's okay. You don't have 
to go out of your way.

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:16.950
You two just do what you want.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:19.750
No, I was thinking of going myself...

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:21.970
It seems like it would be fun to go together.

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:24.840
Well, together, minus one.

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:29.360
Look, you guys both hate each other, right?

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:30.680
Yes, we do.

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:33.060
Even worse than hate, I would say.

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:34.420
There he goes, nitpicking.

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:37.760
And you just want to agree
with everything he says.

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:42.740
Are you sure it doesn't wrap back 
around to you liking each other?

00:09:42.740 --> 00:09:43.850
No!

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:45.900
I mean—

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:47.530
See, you're a perfect match.

00:09:47.530 --> 00:09:49.060
Yeah, right!

00:09:47.530 --> 00:09:49.060
<i>You're mistaken!</i>

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:54.480
<b>Investigation: Zaou Ryuu</b>

00:09:54.050 --> 00:09:55.690
Why is this happening?

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:55.690
<b>Investigation: Naruko Io</b>

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:57.020
That trash!

00:09:57.020 --> 00:10:00.930
It's hard to understand the 
reasoning of commoners and trash.

00:10:00.930 --> 00:10:02.700
Haru-sama. Aki-sama.

00:10:03.070 --> 00:10:05.010
Bamboo tea.

00:10:05.010 --> 00:10:06.620
Oh, bamboo tea.

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:07.970
Thank you.

00:10:07.970 --> 00:10:11.380
I'm surprised an Ape would make something 
as fashionable as bamboo tea.

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:14.390
O-Of course, yes, please call me an ape.

00:10:14.390 --> 00:10:16.630
Just, um... um...

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:18.450
What is it?

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:19.340
How...

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:21.620
How does it feel to be an idol?

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:24.070
What do you mean by that?

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:26.770
<b>Kumano Kuroshiro</b>

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:27.410
I was just wondering what it must be like,

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:30.840
to be loved and admired by everyone...

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:32.870
I'm sorry!

00:10:32.870 --> 00:10:34.900
It's not that I'm jealous of 
you or anything like that!

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:39.360
I've never, ever felt something 
so inappropriate...

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:44.240
Well, maybe once, twice... 23 times...

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:46.360
What?

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:47.790
Then why not be one?

00:10:54.230 --> 00:10:56.710
<i>Welcome to the VEPP Theater.</i>

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:07.470
<i>VEPPer, the twin stars 
racing through the galaxy!</i>

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:10.730
<i>Let's illuminate the mysteries 
of the universe...</i>

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:13.860
<i>On the name of the stars!</i>

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:27.290
<i>VEPPer, the twin stars 
blooming in the galaxy!</i>

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:30.640
<i>Moon and sun, miracles and secrets</i>

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:30.960
The twin stars shining in the heavens!

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:33.980
<i>We're the stars making wishes come true!</i>

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:32.580
Salty Sol!

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:34.500
Melty Luna!

00:11:33.980 --> 00:11:40.580
<i>VEPPer, bringing a thrill 
to this blue planet!</i>

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:38.840
Galaxy Idols, the VEPPer!

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:41.260
Chosen warrior!

00:11:40.580 --> 00:11:43.790
<i>Let's illuminate the entire world!</i>

00:11:41.820 --> 00:11:43.220
Lucky you!

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:45.180
Happy you!

00:11:43.790 --> 00:11:47.140
<i>On the name of the stars!</i>

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:47.500
Shooting...

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:49.170
Star!

00:11:55.220 --> 00:11:57.220
The True Lovracelets...

00:11:58.240 --> 00:12:00.080
A monster, at a time like this?

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:02.130
You think those two will even come?

00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:06.660
Even if they do, they can't fight together 
when they're bickering like that.

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:10.140
We'll just have to make do 
with the three of us, then!

00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:12.160
Let's Love Making!

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:14.570
Love Making!

00:12:18.940 --> 00:12:20.380
The Sparkling Prince!

00:12:21.680 --> 00:12:23.680
Battle Lover Scarlet!

00:12:23.950 --> 00:12:24.930
The Flashing Prince!

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:27.230
Battle Lover Cerulean!

00:12:28.340 --> 00:12:29.780
The Piercing Prince!

00:12:30.190 --> 00:12:31.960
Battle Lover Epinard!

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:35.030
Feel the power...

00:12:35.030 --> 00:12:36.570
Of love!

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:42.860
<b>The Thrilling Prince
Battle Lover Vesta
Finishing Move: Vesta Love Ignit</b>

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:52.120
So cute!

00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:57.920
<i>I'm Panda Monster.</i>

00:12:58.240 --> 00:13:01.720
<i>But although I'm a monster, my 
ultimate move is "cuteness."</i>

00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:04.490
<i>No one can oppose my cuteness.</i>

00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:10.180
So cute!

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:11.670
Bamboo...

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:15.190
So cute!

00:13:16.030 --> 00:13:17.650
It pooped!

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:19.740
So cute!

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:21.110
Don't be fooled!

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:28.030
If you think we'll let you do anything 
because you're cute, you've got another thing coming!

00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:29.630
There they are.

00:13:29.630 --> 00:13:31.840
People jealous of my cuteness.

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:36.340
But I've already prepared for the 
appearance of cowards like you!

00:13:36.340 --> 00:13:38.250
Don't be mean to the panda!

00:13:41.430 --> 00:13:42.550
What?

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:46.790
Is this the cliche yet exciting twist 
where the townspeople turn on the heroes?

00:13:46.790 --> 00:13:49.680
Are they really going to bring that out 
for a pooping panda?

00:13:50.240 --> 00:13:52.510
You can't recover from the two-fold shock!

00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:54.080
You're one to talk!

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:56.120
All you do is poop!

00:13:56.120 --> 00:13:56.940
That's perverted!

00:13:57.120 --> 00:13:58.720
Sh-Shut up!

00:13:58.720 --> 00:14:01.400
My poo is made from bamboo, 
so it doesn't stink!

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:03.400
Take this!

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:04.740
Poo Bomb!

00:14:09.420 --> 00:14:10.060
Oh, come on!

00:14:10.060 --> 00:14:11.540
That's way too straightforward!

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:13.450
Yet we've never faced such 
a dangerous technique!

00:14:14.100 --> 00:14:15.700
Cerulean Love Aqua!

00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:20.130
Epinard Love Hurricane!

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:23.490
Scarlet Love Lumiere!

00:14:31.880 --> 00:14:34.920
The praise of others makes me stronger.

00:14:34.920 --> 00:14:38.060
And jealousy and resentment make me bigger!

00:14:43.470 --> 00:14:44.150
Yumoto!

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:47.690
You're not all that just 
because you're a panda!

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:50.580
Some people do prefer polar bears, you know!

00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:52.120
It's no use, Senpai!

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:56.160
He's that annoying type that will

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:58.660
interpret anything you say as jealousy!

00:14:59.050 --> 00:15:01.630
You're the annoying ones here!

00:15:02.650 --> 00:15:03.820
Take this!

00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:05.340
Bamboo Storm!

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:21.080
Did you know that pandas

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:25.110
sometimes eat mice and other small mammals?

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:29.310
You three are like mice to me!

00:15:29.670 --> 00:15:32.020
Do you understand what I'm getting at?

00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:34.390
Like hell!

00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:40.520
Stop saying stuff we need 
to figure out, poo-face!

00:15:40.520 --> 00:15:42.710
There's no need to understand, anyway!

00:15:42.950 --> 00:15:45.540
Vesta Love Ignit!

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:47.630
Sulfur Love Gaia!

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:54.520
Wh-What is this?

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:56.260
This isn't jealousy or resentment!

00:15:56.630 --> 00:15:59.240
We just don't give a damn about you!

00:15:59.240 --> 00:16:03.350
Although you do need to pay for having the 
nerve to stand against the Battle Lovers.

00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:06.270
Io, you're more aggressive than I thought.

00:16:06.270 --> 00:16:08.480
You're one to talk, Ryuu.

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:11.490
Did you two make up?

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:12.280
Huh?

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:14.570
Certainly not!

00:16:16.650 --> 00:16:18.550
Then what are you doing here?

00:16:19.600 --> 00:16:22.270
They're unrelated incidents!

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:27.100
To hit a cute panda...

00:16:27.100 --> 00:16:29.250
you call yourselves human?!

00:16:29.780 --> 00:16:31.600
You're not even a panda.

00:16:31.600 --> 00:16:33.200
You're a panda monster, y'know?

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:35.720
Just being cute isn't enough!

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:38.310
Running a business means
solving your own problems,

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:41.000
and you must always strive for 
innovation and change!

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:44.200
The road to popularity is a thorny 
path that requires constant hard work!

00:16:44.200 --> 00:16:46.440
Are you prepared to walk that road?!

00:16:47.350 --> 00:16:49.070
Senpais, it's time!

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:52.070
Sparkle, Lumiere of Love!

00:16:54.650 --> 00:16:56.820
Flash, Purifying Aqua!

00:16:57.780 --> 00:17:00.290
Pierce, Gallant Hurricane!

00:17:01.270 --> 00:17:03.500
Roar, Raging Gaia!

00:17:04.430 --> 00:17:06.710
Thrill, Blazing Ignit!

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:13.900
Io-Ryuu-senpai, it's up to you!

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:16.080
Shall we?

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:17.090
Yeah!

00:17:17.320 --> 00:17:19.220
Don't wallow in love!

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:23.830
True Love Attack!

00:17:32.410 --> 00:17:36.040
True Love Fountain!

00:17:49.020 --> 00:17:50.940
Love is over!

00:17:50.940 --> 00:17:53.000
Don't wallow in love, eh?

00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:55.260
You're one to talk.

00:17:55.550 --> 00:17:56.670
You two!

00:17:56.670 --> 00:17:57.940
VEPPer!

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:00.120
The likes of you

00:18:00.120 --> 00:18:02.960
could never understand the thought 
process of someone who is loved.

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:06.400
You lack any qualification 
to speak on the matter.

00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:08.270
In short, you're insufficient.

00:18:08.450 --> 00:18:09.140
Huh?

00:18:09.140 --> 00:18:10.270
What do you mean?

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:12.630
It's not you, the Battle Lovers,

00:18:12.630 --> 00:18:14.980
who are worthy of the love of thousands.

00:18:14.980 --> 00:18:18.420
You'll see that that love is 
reserved for us, VEPPer.

00:18:18.420 --> 00:18:19.450
Little by little.

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:24.960
What was all that, about 
being worthy of love?

00:18:24.960 --> 00:18:29.080
I'm getting the feeling they 
don't like us very much.

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:30.130
Can't put my finger on it.

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:31.840
<b>Earth Defense Club (lol)</b>

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:42.230
Yumoto's engaged in repetitive behavior.

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:46.720
Like a stressed wolf at the zoo.

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:48.060
Come on, Ryuu, Io.

00:18:48.260 --> 00:18:50.180
Get a grip already.

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:52.110
I'm sorry, Yufuin-senpai.

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:54.620
I'm a very petty person.

00:18:54.620 --> 00:18:57.630
I know I'm worse than Io.

00:18:58.260 --> 00:19:00.030
I'm an idiot who only thinks 
about getting with girls.

00:19:00.300 --> 00:19:02.140
What are you talking about?

00:19:02.490 --> 00:19:05.590
Your dating habits stimulate the economy.

00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:08.030
It's worthy of praise.

00:19:08.420 --> 00:19:10.040
Your investments are way more amazing.

00:19:10.760 --> 00:19:13.900
You're committed to the 
development of your business.

00:19:13.900 --> 00:19:17.010
My little dates are nothing compared to that.

00:19:17.220 --> 00:19:20.260
No, in the end, the economy 
comes down to people.

00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:22.930
The economy can't function if 
people don't go about their lives.

00:19:23.340 --> 00:19:25.700
That's what you're doing.

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:28.570
You're much more amazing!

00:19:28.570 --> 00:19:29.420
Acknowledge it already!

00:19:29.420 --> 00:19:30.530
I will not!

00:19:30.530 --> 00:19:33.100
Ryuu, you should have confidence instead!

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:35.030
Shut up, you genius!

00:19:35.030 --> 00:19:37.570
Give it a rest already, you icon!

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:39.530
Wait a minute!

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:40.630
What?

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:42.100
Are those backhanded compliments?

00:19:42.100 --> 00:19:44.710
Or do you actually both think 
the world of each other?

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:46.030
Yes, I do!

00:19:46.260 --> 00:19:47.250
It's just that he...

00:19:47.250 --> 00:19:48.390
You...

00:19:48.390 --> 00:19:49.750
...won't admit it!

00:19:51.240 --> 00:19:53.040
Oh, I have a question!

00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:54.710
How did this start?

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:57.130
Because the other boys in 
class were making fun of him!

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:02.720
That's why I was explaining 
how amazing Io was!

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:05.640
I explained it to them, kindly and concisely!

00:20:06.010 --> 00:20:08.470
But Io overheard it and denied it!

00:20:08.470 --> 00:20:11.890
Because I lack even 1/10th of your value!

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:13.330
But I told you!

00:20:13.330 --> 00:20:14.390
You're amazing!

00:20:14.390 --> 00:20:15.520
Why won't you acknowledge it?

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:17.020
I'm not amazing!

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:19.280
Amazing! Amazing! Amazing!

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:19.280
What's so amazing about me?!

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:22.990
This is freaking dumb!!!

00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:24.590
I just remembered.

00:20:24.590 --> 00:20:27.640
When you came to the Kurotama 
Bath for the first time,

00:20:27.640 --> 00:20:28.950
it was just like this.

00:20:29.210 --> 00:20:30.660
Yeah, right!

00:20:29.210 --> 00:20:30.660
You're mistaken!

00:20:33.440 --> 00:20:35.050
This is the worst.

00:20:33.440 --> 00:20:35.050
This stinks.

00:20:35.050 --> 00:20:36.880
Excuse me, sirs.

00:20:37.180 --> 00:20:39.480
We can dry your uniforms quickly.

00:20:39.480 --> 00:20:41.940
In the meantime, please, get in the bath.

00:20:46.610 --> 00:20:48.150
What on Earth?

00:20:48.150 --> 00:20:50.840
How pushy can you get?

00:20:54.510 --> 00:20:56.240
Not bad at all, huh?

00:20:56.240 --> 00:20:57.690
Yeah, pretty good.

00:20:57.980 --> 00:21:00.870
I guess we can agree on some things.

00:21:00.870 --> 00:21:02.650
I'm pretty shocked, too.

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:06.040
Well, I guess they're both in the club.

00:21:06.040 --> 00:21:07.660
Are you okay with that?

00:21:07.970 --> 00:21:08.770
Yeah!

00:21:09.640 --> 00:21:12.780
In retrospect, I'm grateful 
for that splash of water.

00:21:12.780 --> 00:21:16.960
Without that, they might have 
never spoken to each other again.

00:21:17.340 --> 00:21:18.840
What's wrong?

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:20.300
I'm sorry!

00:21:20.510 --> 00:21:24.760
The one who splashed you was probably me!

00:21:28.160 --> 00:21:31.530
The ridge tiles on a bathhouse are 
guardian spirits against fire!

00:21:31.530 --> 00:21:33.730
Thanks for all your help!

00:21:34.050 --> 00:21:37.900
But we're a natural hot spring, 
so there's no danger of fire!

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:39.150
Oh well!

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:41.460
Yumoto.

00:21:43.760 --> 00:21:46.740
I need you to wash these 
and iron them quickly.

00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:51.240
Big bro, are these from Binan High School?

00:21:52.690 --> 00:21:54.700
That's the time you were 
talking about, right?

00:21:55.020 --> 00:21:58.880
I think I need to apologize to you both.

00:21:59.120 --> 00:22:00.480
Huh? What?

00:22:00.480 --> 00:22:02.530
We're the ones who should apologize.

00:22:02.530 --> 00:22:04.970
For bringing down the mood in the club room.

00:22:04.970 --> 00:22:06.380
Not that!

00:22:06.780 --> 00:22:10.350
Because I was hasty with 
the iron, the lining...

00:22:14.250 --> 00:22:15.520
I'm sorry!

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:16.780
That was you?!

00:22:16.780 --> 00:22:18.760
I always wondered...

00:22:18.760 --> 00:22:19.800
Now, now.

00:22:19.800 --> 00:22:22.520
It means you match me! It's premiere!

00:22:22.820 --> 00:22:24.940
I'm not happy about that at all!

00:22:25.260 --> 00:22:26.940
What did you say?!

00:22:27.260 --> 00:22:30.280
Love shock!

00:24:00.890 --> 00:24:05.730
A Christmas of Love and Miracles

00:24:00.890 --> 00:24:05.730
Next Time

00:24:01.700 --> 00:24:04.220
Next time: "A Christmas of 
Love and Miracles!"

00:24:04.220 --> 00:24:05.720
Love Making!
